 "summary": "A blank string ('' or whitespace, what isMissing reads as missing) on a field whose declared type is in the spec's NON_TEXT_STORED_VALUE_TYPES (number, currency, percent, rating, slider, progress, summary, boolean, toggle, date, datetime, time) now becomes null at the start of ObjectQL.insert() / update(). The same happens at the same point in validate(), the dry run. The door does it before the middleware, the caller snapshots, the defaults, the hooks, the strips and validation. The rule is one function, normalizeBlankTypedValues in record-validator.ts; there is no REST or driver copy, and every REST, batch and import door reaches the engine through those methods. Measured on memory, SQLite and live PostgreSQL across 11 engine and REST doors: base stored '' (memory, SQLite) or was refused by the driver (PostgreSQL 22P02 / 22007, REST 500); head stores null everywhere. Text, lookup and select '' are byte-identical base to head, as are valid values and existing refusals. The number branch now reads NUMERIC_VALUE_TYPES, so 'abc' on progress or summary answers invalid_number; only the type check was added, and no bound or scale. Defaults: a blank now takes a defaultValue on insert exactly as null does. That changed one verdict: a required-with-default blank was refused as required and now takes the default. Consequence reported: a summary roll-up doing min/max over a temporal child field is now refused at recompute on memory and SQLite (ERR_SUMMARY_RECOMPUTE), as it already was on PostgreSQL.",
